The raw pool table holds 1 << 13 entries instead of 1 << 12, as seedds/nxnative's host table does: Ocarina of Time reaches
about 3,600 ranges in a couple of minutes of play and went past the 4,095 the old table held in the longer sessions, where
the host dropped the pools that no longer fit and logged them (their addresses then read 0 through the raw path). The host
fills the table once per pool generation, so twice the memory (256 KiB) and one more step for a search that only runs when
the last-entry word misses cost nothing measurable. The host's GMEM_MAP_ENTRIES must change with it (nvn_mtl.m gmem_map_gpu),
and the cache name with the translation.

--- a/src/Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader/Translation/Optimizations/GlobalToStorage.cs	2026-11-09 04:17:58
+++ b/src/Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader/Translation/Optimizations/GlobalToStorage.cs	2026-11-09 05:01:47
@@ -883,9 +883,12 @@
 
